id: pm-ksv2
title: "Sentry captures deliberate Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D interrupts as error-level events (AbortError, PM-CLI-27)"
description: Classify deliberate SIGINT and readline cancellations as handled control flow so user aborts do not create error-level Sentry issues or block release telemetry gates.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,sentry,telemetry
created_at: "2026-07-12T08:08:23.019Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T16:10:52.588Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T16:09:52.233Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T16:09:52.233Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "user-initiated SIGINT/Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D aborts are classified as handled non-error telemetry (breadcrumb or info event, or not captured at all); AbortError from readline/prompt cancellation no longer creates unresolved error-level Sentry issues; the sentry-telemetry gate cannot be blocked by an explicit user terminal cancellation; regression coverage preserves observability for unrelated AbortError failures"
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: low
confidence: high
release: v2026.7.14
resolution: Extended capture-time user-intent classification from Ctrl+C/SIGINT to explicit Ctrl+D readline AbortError while preserving capture for unrelated abort failures.
expected_result: "Deliberate Ctrl+C, Ctrl+D, and SIGINT terminal cancellation does not create error-level Sentry issues or block release telemetry gates."
actual_result: "Source and built runtime classify AbortError 'Aborted with Ctrl+D' as non-capturable; focused PM-linked tests, the 7,508-test exact coverage suite, graph/record gates, and a real PTY Ctrl+D reproduction pass. The already-published 2026.8.17 release remains affected and PM-CLI-27 remains unresolved until this fix is merged and published."
affected_version: 2026.8.17
fixed_version: unreleased
regression: true
