  "2026-07-12T15:41:03.486Z",maintainer-agent,"Recurrence evidence 2026-07-12T15:36Z: this performance run interrupted an unintended interactive pm init prompt with Ctrl+C after pm test used schema context. Sentry correctly received PM-CLI-27 as handled=true but still reopened it at error/high; the linked runner was rerun successfully with --pm-context tracker. This is the same deliberate-abort class already owned here, not a new defect. Resolving the event group again pending the capture-time class fix."
  "2026-07-13T19:42:45.175Z",codex-root,"Live recurrence evidence 2026-07-13: release gate reports PM-CLI-27 unresolved high with count=5 and last seen 2026-07-13T16:46Z. During this lane, two linked-test attempts with an unintended interactive TTY reached the pm init wizard and were deliberately cancelled with Ctrl+C, reproducing the already-owned handled AbortError class; the non-TTY tracker-context rerun completed. No duplicate item created or claimed."
  "2026-07-14T00:09:48.869Z",codex-gpt5,"Implementation evidence: Sentry capture now recognizes user-initiated AbortError Ctrl+C/SIGINT control flow without suppressing unrelated abort failures. Dedicated regressions and all exact-tree strict gates pass at 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-07-14T00:29:12.745Z",codex-root,"Final verification: pm linked Sentry control-flow suite passes with sandbox parity; live PM-CLI-27 is resolved and the reliability gate reports zero blocking high/critical issues with healthy telemetry."
  "2026-08-17T15:42:16.208Z","harness:codex","Live recurrence evidence: Sentry PM-CLI-27 regressed at 2026-08-17T11:28:33Z on pm-cli@2026.8.17 with AbortError 'Aborted with Ctrl+D', handled=yes, system-only readline frames, but pm.error_code=unclassified_runtime_error. The 14-day sentry-telemetry gate reports critical=0 high=1 and blocks. This is the same deliberate terminal-abort class as the closed Ctrl+C fix, so no duplicate item was created. Extend capture-time intent classification to explicit Ctrl+D only; unrelated AbortError remains observable."
  "2026-08-17T16:09:16.947Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence 2026-08-17: TDD reproduced the exact Sentry event message before the policy change, then the PM-linked control-flow suite passed (3 tests). A solo full coverage run passed 515 files / 7,508 tests at statements 54,687/54,687, branches 40,815/40,815, functions 11,245/11,245, lines 52,784/52,784. Repository lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static assurance, package boundary/parity, surface replication, SDK import costs, and all graph/record assertions; the aggregate run's loaded transport benchmark exceeded its 362 ms get ceiling by 2 ms, and an immediate isolated no-load rerun passed all 6 operations. Manual PTY test in /tmp/pm-ctrl-d-manual.OHiASS reached the init wizard, Ctrl+D produced 'Aborted with Ctrl+D' and exit 1, and the built classifier returned sentry_capture=false for the corresponding named AbortError. Dependabot and code-scanning report zero open alerts. GitHub secret-scanning is currently returning provider HTTP 503, so no result is claimed. PM-CLI-27 is intentionally not resolved yet because public 2026.8.17 remains affected; resolve only after merged/published verification."
